        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-07T16:21:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think I have heard Jett say that on our EC platforms, int reads and writes are functionally atomic. If that\u0027s true, and if the reads of last_read always take place in interrupt context, and if the value of last_read will be explicitly invalid before the mux op completes, I guess there is not a race here.",
